# What never enters the build context.
#
# Everything here is excluded from the context Docker sends to the daemon, so
# these files cannot reach any stage of the build — not even a layer that is
# later discarded, where a leaked credential would still sit in the build cache.

# --- Secrets. The reason this file matters. -------------------------------
#
# No environment file may enter an image: configuration is supplied at run
# time with `-e` / `--env-file`, and AWS credentials come from the provider
# chain. The image does not set the only build-time variable,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLASSMIND_PUBLIC_DEMO (a non-secret flag). See
# docs/configuration.md.
.env*
.aws/
*.pem
*.key
credentials

# --- Build output and caches ----------------------------------------------
#
# `next build` runs inside the image. A host `.next` would be copied in and
# then overwritten, and a host `node_modules` may hold platform-specific
# binaries built for Windows.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
.swc/

# --- Tests -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The running server never touches them. `tests/fixtures/demo-lecture.md` is
# read only by `npm run seed:aws`, which is a host-side operation against AWS —
# see the note in docs/aws-setup.md. Delete these two lines if you ever want to
# seed from inside the container.
tests/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
coverage/
vitest.config.ts

# --- Version control, editors, tooling -------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.kiro/
eslint.config.mjs
lint.json

# --- Logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
tree.txt
probe.txt
lint-*.txt

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
*.md
docs/
# …except the synthetic demo lecture, which local mode builds the demo class from.
!lib/demo/demo-lecture.md

# --- Local-mode data (embedded store, uploads) — never baked into an image --
.classmind/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- Docker's own files ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Editing the Dockerfile should not invalidate the layer that copies the source.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.vercel/
